# Frontend settings. Everything starting with VITE_ is PUBLIC (it is built into the JavaScript every visitor downloads).
# Never put a password, database address or secret in this file or in a VITE_ variable on Vercel;
# the build stops with an error if it finds one.
#
# Local development: leave this unset. The Vite dev server forwards /api to the backend on port 3001.
#
# Production (Vercel): set VITE_API_URL in the Vercel project settings to the public address of the backend,
# https and no trailing slash, for example:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://your-service.onrender.com
# The backend must then list your Vercel address in CLIENT_ORIGINS (see DEPLOYMENT.md).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
